        "calls": 2,
        "title": "Native app client events, admission status, and publish failure codes",
        "summary": "The common package adds a new module, common/src/analytics/client-events.ts, that defines the wire contract for native iOS and Android app events ingested via the POST /api/v1/client-events endpoint, including per-event property schemas and a batch limit of 50 events. In parallel, the CLI admission flow now records a structured admission_status property on failed model requests, mapping session failures to tokens like request_timeout or paywall so telemetry distinguishes the cause of a refusal. The Sites publish subsystem gains a closed set of SITE_PUBLISH_FAILURE_CODES and a failure_code field on error results, letting analytics break down publish failures by reason instead of free-text messages. The product funnel schema also widens its surface enum to include ios and android, and new analytics event constants for mobile app opens, reviews, pushes, features, and crash reports are registered in the shared AnalyticsEvent enum.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "maintainers",
        "evidence": "New file common/src/analytics/client-events.ts defines the wire contract for POST /api/v1/client-events with constants like CLIENT_EVENTS_MAX_EVENTS = 50. cli/src/hooks/use-freebuff-chat-admission.ts adds sessionFailureStatus to map failures to admission_status, and common/src/sites/publish-events.ts introduces SITE_PUBLISH_FAILURE_CODES and failure_code fields.",
        "userVisible": false,
        "confidence": "medium",
        "unknowns": "The diff does not show the server-side route that consumes POST /api/v1/client-events or the app code that emits these events, so rollout state of the mobile pipeline is not visible here.",
